# SR-IOV VF device ownership for unprivileged LXCs
# Deployed to: /etc/udev/rules.d/99-sriov-lxc.rules on winston
#
# After Nextcloud/Immich migration to Flatcar VM 100, VF 1 and VF 2
# are no longer assigned to LXCs. Only Plex (LXC 105) uses the PF
# in privileged mode (no udev rules needed).
#
# VF 0 (00:02.1) → VM 100 (Flatcar) — passed via Proxmox PCI device
# VF 1-6 → available
#
# If new unprivileged LXCs need GPU access in the future:
#   1. Inside LXC: grep render /etc/group  → e.g., render:x:108
#   2. Check idmap: grep "lxc.idmap" /etc/pve/lxc/<CTID>.conf → offset (usually 100000)
#   3. Host GID = offset + container GID  → 100000 + 108 = 100108
